   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The home and the building",
     "texto": [
      "Today we talk about decorating a home and the building you live in.\n\n- **Decorating:** with an **alfombra** on the floor, **cortinas** at the window, a picture on the wall and a **florero** with flowers.\n- **The bedroom:** the bed, the wardrobe, the **cómoda** and the **mesilla de noche**.\n- **The kitchen:** the fridge and the **congelador**, the oven, the **cafetera**. An appliance is **enchufado** (plugged in) and unplugged.\n- **The building:** the **portero** looks after the entrance. The **propietario** is the owner of the flat and the casero rents it out. A bright, **soleado** flat is very pleasant. Below there may be an **aparcamiento**.\n- **Letters:** on the envelope go the addressee and the **remitente**. At the end of the letter you can add a postscript."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Where each thing is",
     "texto": [
      "To say where a piece of furniture goes or where something is, use these expressions:\n\n- **encima de** / **debajo de** (on top of / under): la lámpara está **encima de** la mesilla; la alfombra va **debajo de** la mesa.\n- **delante de** / **detrás de** (in front of / behind): el sofá está **delante de** la ventana.\n- **al lado de** / **junto a** (next to): la cafetera está **junto al** frigorífico.\n- **entre** (between): la cómoda está **entre** la cama y la ventana.\n- **enfrente de** (opposite): el portero vive **enfrente del** ascensor.\n\nRemember: **de + el = del** and **a + el = al**: debajo **del** edificio, junto **al** frigorífico."
     ],
